From: Kenichi Kamiya <kachick1@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] attach: fork into container PID namespace before exec

Calling setns(CLONE_NEWPID) does not change the caller's PID namespace;
only children created by subsequent fork() calls enter the new namespace.
Without fork(), the attached interactive shell runs in the host PID namespace
while its child processes run in the container PID namespace.
When an interactive shell (e.g. bash) invokes setpgid() for job control,
the Linux kernel returns EPERM because the target and caller reside in
different PID namespaces.

Fork before calling exec_in_overlay(), let the child exec, and wait for it
in the parent to propagate its exit status.
---
 src/attach/child.rs | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/attach/child.rs b/src/attach/child.rs
index 854cdf7..28662b2 100644
--- a/src/attach/child.rs
+++ b/src/attach/child.rs
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ use crate::paths;
 use crate::procfs::ProcStatus;
 use crate::pty;
 use crate::syscalls::mount_api::make_mount_idmapped;
+use crate::syscalls::process::{fork, Fork};
 
 const RECURSIVE_CLONE: OpenTreeFlags =
     OpenTreeFlags::OPEN_TREE_CLONE.union(OpenTreeFlags::AT_RECURSIVE);
@@ -458,10 +459,23 @@ pub(crate) fn run(options: &mut ChildOptions) -> Result<std::convert::Infallible
         profile.inherit_profile()?;
     }
 
-    // Step 12: Execute the command
-    // This will replace the current process (attach child) with the shell
-    // When the shell exits, the parent will see it and exit accordingly
-    // Use exec_in_overlay() since we're in the overlay environment with access
-    // to both host binaries and container filesystem
-    Ok(cmd.exec_in_overlay()?)
+    // Step 12: Fork into container PID namespace before executing command
+    match fork().map_err(AttachError::Fork)? {
+        Fork::Child => {
+            cmd.exec_in_overlay()?;
+            unreachable!()
+        }
+        Fork::ParentOf(child_pid) => {
+            let mut status = 0;
+            unsafe {
+                libc::waitpid(child_pid.as_raw_nonzero().get(), &mut status, 0);
+            }
+            if libc::WIFEXITED(status) {
+                std::process::exit(libc::WEXITSTATUS(status));
+            } else if libc::WIFSIGNALED(status) {
+                std::process::exit(128 + libc::WTERMSIG(status));
+            }
+            std::process::exit(1);
+        }
+    }
 }
